1. Wrap the child in `React.memo` (so it checks for prop changes).
2. Ensure the object reference stays exactly the same between renders.

Here are the three ways to handle the object reference, depending on your setup:

#### Solution 1: Move the object outside the component (If the object is static)
If the object never changes and doesn't rely on state or props, simply move it outside the parent component. It will only be created once.

